 The P-384 half, produced the same way: OpenSSL 3.2.4 signed the same 130
 bytes with a secp384r1 key under SHA-384, and .NET verified the result
 from this same SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER. The signature is 102 bytes of
 DER rather than 71, because each integer is forty-eight bytes wide.

